  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Given below are two statements related to Ellingham diagram :</p><p>Statement I : Ellingham diagrams can be constructed for formation of oxides, sulphides and halides of metals.</p><p>Statement II : It consists of plots of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#916;H</mi><mo>&#176;</mo></math>&nbsp;vs <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi></math> for formation of oxides of elements.</p><p>In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :</p>",
    "image": null
  },
