  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>An Ellingham diagram is a graph showing the temperature dependence of the stability of compounds.&nbsp;Ellingham diagrams can be drawn for Sulphides, Oxides and Halides. The Ellingham diagram is a graph that shows how the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#916;G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mn>0</mn></msubsup></math> varies with temperature as a result of the formation of elemental oxides.</p>",
    "image": null
